From ca504108720e7a91af6df60f17a9e21879fe71be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wjxn13 <236573882+wjxn13@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 23:01:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] test(core): cover mention routing, agent labels and
 queued messages

Adds offline coverage for the addressing layer introduced in the previous
commit. No production code is touched.

* config/agent_label_test.go -- `EffectiveAgentLabel` resolution order
  (project `label` overrides global `agent_label`), the `{label}` placeholder,
  and the empty/whitespace cases that must render to "" rather than a bare
  prefix.

* core/agent_label_test.go -- `stampAgentLabel` is applied once and only once,
  is skipped for empty content, and leaves content untouched when no label is
  configured.

* core/mention_route_test.go -- the gate decision table: message naming a peer
  is dropped, message naming self passes, unaddressed message passes, and the
  first @token wins when a message names more than one project. Also pins the
  alias matching rules (case folding, leading whitespace, `@` optional) and the
  longest-alias-prefix match, so "@dsh" does not get shadowed by a shorter
  alias that happens to be a prefix of it.

* core/mention_sticky_test.go -- sticky addressee lifecycle: refreshed by an
  addressed message, consumed by a following text-less (media) message,
  expired by TTL, and never applied to a message that carries text.

* core/queued_message_test.go -- the queued-message confirmation composes the
  base sentence, the queue detail block and (only when peer agents exist) the
  reroute hint, in the right order and without a dangling blank line.

Run: `go test ./core/ ./config/`
